      "q": "Practice: delete a todo",
      "a": "Summary\nSummary: delete a todo. Filter out the id. This is a hands-on lab, not a riddle. You should be able to explain the function out loud, then type it from memory. What the code is doing: Walk the snippet like this: `todos = todos.filter((t) => t.id !== id` — Delete — drop this id. A line you can point at: function removeTodo(id) { In an interview, start with the job in plain words (the first sentences here), then walk the snippet. Do not start with a shop story. When you are done: run it, break it with empty input or a wrong id, then fix the check. That is the whole point of a practice row. The list shrinks by one. Other ids stay. Interviewers want ownership: only the owner or an admin. Never delete by position 0 after a sort. Confirm on the UI, enforce on the server. 404 if missing, 403 if not yours. Name Create/Read/Update/Delete if this is a list, or 401 vs 403 if this is login.\n\nThe problem before\nSplice by index deleted the wrong row after a sort. A guest called DELETE and wiped someone else's todo. There was no 403. This lab exists because that failure is what interviews and real apps hit. Filter out the id. Never delete by position 0 after a sort. Confirm on the UI, enforce on the server. 404 if missing, 403 if not yours.\n\nWhat this is\nFilter out the id. Delete means drop the row with that id. filter in JS. DELETE /todos/:id. SQL DELETE FROM todos WHERE id = $1 AND user_id = $2. Then Read again so the UI matches. Walk the snippet like this: `todos = todos.filter((t) => t.id !== id` — Delete — drop this id. The list shrinks by one. Other ids stay. Interviewers want ownership: only the owner or an admin.\n\nWhat it solves\nThe list shrinks by one. Other ids stay. Interviewers want ownership: only the owner or an admin. After this row you can demo the happy path and one failed path (empty input, wrong password, or missing id). Filter out the id. Say the job in one sentence, then point at the code, then name one mistake.\n\nReal-life example\nA lost-and-found shelf. You remove the tag with ticket 42. You do not sweep every bag. Ticket 43 is still there. Map guest → user, counter → this function, back room → the array, file, or database in the snippet. delete a todo. Say the job in one sentence, then point at the code, then name one mistake.\n\nUses\nRemove todo, destroy card, DELETE route, unsubscribe. Soft-delete with deleted_at is the same idea with a flag. On this sheet, the question is: Practice: delete a todo. Use the same idea in the next lab instead of copying a new pattern. The list shrinks by one. Other ids stay. Interviewers want ownership: only the owner or an admin.\n\nWatch out\nNever delete by position 0 after a sort. Confirm on the UI, enforce on the server. 404 if missing, 403 if not yours. Read the comments on the right before you paste. If a line looks clever and has no comment, it is the line that will fail in an interview. Filter out the id.",
